    "check": "returned unopposed: the seven retiring members signed a joint address thanking the electors 'for returning them again', and all seven appear in the attendance list of the new council's first meeting (Northern Herald, 21 May 1938, p. 6)",
    "url": "https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/search/results/1938-05-14/1938-05-14?basicsearch=bangor"
  },
  "note": "Municipal election, 16 May 1938. The Northern Herald of 14 May 1938, p. 3, prints a joint address from seven retiring members — Bowman, Cathy, Gray, Logan, McCartney, MacCullagh and Milligan — thanking the electors for returning them again, so these seven were returned without a contest. The first meeting of the new council, in the same paper of 21 May 1938, p. 6, lists the members present: the Mayor, Alderman Dr. R. M. Bowman (who arrived shortly after the start); Aldermen Gray, Bailie, Cathy and M'Cullagh; and Councillors Walter Malcolm, W. J. Bailie, J. S. M'Cullough, T. Henderson, George M'Cartney, S. H. Forrest, T. Brice Smyth, R. H. Hamilton, Lt.-Col. Porter, M.C., C. F. Milligan, F. Logan, W. H. M'Millan, M.A., Campbell and Davidson. The address prints 'McCartney' and the attendance list 'M'Cartney'; they are treated as the same member. Where the source gives no initials, none are supplied. No poll figures were printed for the election. Returned unopposed."
